Place 1 into chart.
Keep a shared rows as 0.
Keep a shared columns as 0.
Set rows to 2.
Set columns to 2.
Keep a shared labels as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared sizes as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared tint as 0.
Keep a shared count as 0.
For every spot from 0 to 3.
Place -1 into labels.

To paint from node (a whole number).
If item node of chart is 0, return.
If item node of labels is not -1, return.
Set item node of labels to tint.
Add 1 to count.
The row is node divided by columns.
The column is node modulo columns.
If row is more than 0, paint from node minus columns.
If row is less than rows minus 1, paint from node plus columns.
If column is more than 0, paint from node minus 1.
If column is less than columns minus 1, paint from node plus 1.

For every node from 0 to 3.
If item node of chart is 1 and item node of labels is -1.
Set count to 0.
Paint from node.
Place count into sizes.
Set tint to tint plus 1.

The best is 0.
For every node from 0 to 3.
If item node of chart is 0.
The near is an empty list of whole numbers.
The row is node divided by columns.
The column is node modulo columns.
If row is more than 0 and item (node minus columns) of chart is 1, Place item (node minus columns) of labels into near.
If row is less than rows minus 1 and item (node plus columns) of chart is 1, Place item (node plus columns) of labels into near.
If column is more than 0 and item (node minus 1) of chart is 1, Place item (node minus 1) of labels into near.
If column is less than columns minus 1 and item (node plus 1) of chart is 1, Place item (node plus 1) of labels into near.
The candidate is 1.
If candidate is more than best, set best to candidate.
The seen is an empty list of whole numbers.
For each label in near.
If seen contains label, skip to the next one.
Place label into seen.
The gain is item label of sizes.
Add gain to candidate.
If candidate is more than best, set best to candidate.

If best is 0, set best to rows times columns.
Show best.
